// Title: Taskmgr as LOCAL_SYSTEM
// Sigma ID: 9fff585c-c33e-4a86-b3cd-39312079a65f
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2018-03-18 | Modified: 2022-05-27
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1036
// Description: Detects the creation of taskmgr.exe process in context of LOCAL_SYSTEM
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - Internal Research
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_taskmgr_localsystem.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (AccountName contains "AUTHORI" or AccountName contains "AUTORI") and FolderPath endswith "\\taskmgr.exe"
